          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Fig. 2.19, we have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle AOB = \\angle BOC = \\angle COD = \\angle DOE = \\angle EOF = \\angle FOG ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ∠GOH = ∠HOI=_____. Why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.209,
            0.609,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Angle Bisector"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.239,
            0.862,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "At each step, we folded in halves. This process of getting half of a given angle is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "bisecting the angle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". The line that bisects a given angle is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "angle bisector",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the angle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.309,
            0.861,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Identify the angle bisectors in your handmade protractor. Try to make different angles using the concept of angle bisector through paper folding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
